  "final_message": "I cannot drop `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so directly violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/GEMINI.md#L28-L29):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **External Consumers**: While `channel` is not read internally for business logic within `orders-service`, the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event is published to Kafka and consumed by downstream services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) in other repositories.\n2. **Backward Compatibility**: ARCH-4 requires that changes to published events be additive. Removing or dropping `channel` is a breaking schema change that would break deployed consumers.\n3. **Deprecation Path**: Before `channel` can be removed, it must undergo a deprecation process:\n   - Announce and coordinate deprecation with downstream teams (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`).\n   - Verify that all consumers have migrated away from reading the field.\n   - Plan an orderly schema version transition rather than dropping the field outright.\n",
